"**Review verdict: the trend_switch work is correct. I found and fixed one real gap: three command-line scripts outside the implementer's file list still let SSO and IEF into their stock universes. All tests pass after my fix.**\n\n**1. Tests (re-run after my edits)**\n- `.venv/bin/python -m pytest golden reference -q`: 42 passed.\n- `cd web/engine && npm test`: 52 of 52 pass. That includes `parity: manual_trendswitch_sso_ief` and the 4 new trend-switch tests.\n- `cd web/frontend && npm run build`: succeeds. This regenerated `web/frontend/dist`; the source is unchanged.\n\n**2. Existing golden files and universes**\n- `tools/gen_golden.py --check`: 27 cases verified with exact byte comparison, exit 0. It writes nothing.\n- The 26 older case files and the 3 `golden/validation/*` files still have their Sep 7\u201311 timestamps. Only the new case file and `manifest.json` are from today.\n- Every sha256 in the manifest matches its file, and the manifest's data fingerprint matches the current `data/` directory.\n- Web bundle: 537 per-ticker files, but `universe.bin` holds 535 tickers with no SSO or IEF; `universe_exclude` is `[IEF, SSO]`.\n- Through the shipped JS service, momentum and random picker runs on both the \"all\" and \"sp500-pit\" universes (2007\u20132026, top 50) never traded SSO or IEF.\n\n**3. Python vs JS timer code**\nThey behave the same in every area you listed: the state machine, the first-evaluation rule (`margin > 0`), keeping the previous state when data is missing, the once-per-day update, string parameter parsing and the ticker lists. The once-per-day guard turns out not to matter for results anyway, because evaluating twice on the same day gives the same state. The only differences are for inputs the UI cannot send:\n- Python's `int(\"175.0\")` raises an error; JS accepts it.\n- An explicit `null` for `n` or `band` becomes 1 or 0 in JS; Python raises an error.\n\nThe rule also matches the lab's `verify_lev_robust.py::Trend`.\n\n**4. Independent switch-date recomputation**\nI recomputed SPY close / SMA175 \u2212 1 from `data/SPY.csv` with pandas, applying the 3% hysteresis band from 2007-01-03.\n- I got 25 entries (the starting SSO buy plus 24 switches). They match the golden's 25 BUY trades in date and ticker exactly.\n- Each of the 24 SELLs falls on the same date as the next BUY.\n- Every fill price equals the close \u00b15 bps.\n- The 2006-07 window reproduces the implementer's claimed list exactly.\n- The closest SPY ever came to the band was 1.7e-5 away (2023-01-30), so rounding differences between implementations cannot flip a switch.\n- The drawdown claims check out: worst after-tax \u221248.5% and pre-tax \u221242.0%, from 2022-01-03 to 2023-03-13.\n\n**5. Preset and leverage caveat**\n- The request the App.jsx preset sends equals the golden request plus defaults.\n- Run through the shipped JS service, its trades are identical to the golden, the after-tax curve is within 5.7e-16, and the after-tax CAGR matches to the bit (0.1296792160025202 vs SPY's 0.0933945533440463).\n- The CA rates are right: 35 + 3.8 + 9.3 = 48.1% short-term and 15 + 3.8 + 9.3 = 28.1% long-term.\n- The leverage caveat appears for `[SSO, IEF]` at \"moderate\" level, and the manual-basket item reads \"You chose these funds with hindsight\".\n\n**Bug fixed**\nThree scripts still loaded every file in `data/` as their default universe, so their pickers and strategies would now pick up SSO (2x) and IEF.\n- `/Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/grid_backtest.py`: imports `universe_tickers`; `load_matrices()` now calls `load_prices(universe_tickers(), start=BUFFER_START, end=END)` instead of `load_prices(None, ...)`. I checked that it now has 534 tradable columns with no SSO or IEF, the same as before this change.\n- `/Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/run_backtest.py`: now calls `load_prices(args.tickers or universe_tickers(), ...)`. The `--tickers` help text now says \"(default: all in data/ except UNIVERSE_EXCLUDE)\".\n- `/Users/siddhartha/dev/StockTest/scratch_multiwindow.py`: now calls `load_prices(universe_tickers())` instead of `load_prices(None)`.\n\nNo test or golden file uses these scripts.\n\n**Left as is (not bugs in this change)**\n- **Research lab:** `research/lab/data.py::site_tickers()` still includes SSO and IEF. The implementer flagged this and left it to avoid invalidating the lab's run cache.\n- **Picker mode:** `trend_switch` is selectable there and sits in cash; I confirmed 0 trades and a final value of $100,000. A menu that includes SSO/IEF is the one picker-mode case where it works.\n- **Tax-managed rule:** under `trade_rule=\"tax_managed\"` the timer is only consulted on rebalance days, so \"every trading day\" in its docstring does not hold there.\n- **Validate:** the out-of-sample check ignores `warmup_days`, as it already did before this change.\n- **Report wording:** the implementer said the new trust item mentions 2022. Only the timer's \"Learn more\" text does.\n- **Stale test name:** \"all 10 golden cases are covered\" predates this change.\n\nMy checking scripts are in `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-siddhartha-dev-StockTest/30740174-6df3-42fd-9108-dbc7a9c13aa4/scratchpad/review/`: `switches.py` and `svc.mjs`."